    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0682" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/97: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-02T18:00:00-05:00">January 2, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Your 894, December 24, 5 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d559-f1"/> On December 22
                    Commander in-Chief Asiatic Fleet<anchor n="12" xml:id="d559-f2"/> was authorized
                    to withdraw the marine forces from Tientsin on transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henderson</hi> latter part of January, first transferring from those forces
                    sufficient men to bring Shanghai regiment and Legation Guard to full strength.
                    Department regrets that you were not informed in due course.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
